{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RP20 independently verified and conditionally approved on 2026-09-01 at audited snapshot 9a94ef9737fbdf070ae314bba6e797319aee2301. The read-only background reviewer did not consult the Janitor report and confirmed all four claims: stale rollout/module prose conflicts with live mapping, Jira DC, ACLI/ADF, and create/update paths (`mapping_config.py:3,18`; `adapters/__init__.py:3,15`; `adapters/jira/__init__.py:3`; `apply_outbound.py:80`; `_backend.py:218`); `outbound_differ.py:7` overstates local ownership because five inbound-mirrored fields suppress outbound writes when local equals the stored baseline (`outbound_field_diff.py:39,263,330`, pinned by `test_live_path_direction_preservation_e6e9.py:128,165`); `OutboundDiffConfig` prose lists five inputs while the dataclass has nine behavior-bearing fields (`outbound_differ.py:221,239,520`); and `docs/env-vars.md:149,153` lacks the accepted values, defaults, and effects implemented at `create_route.py:70` and `reconcile_helpers.py:653`.\n\nTicketization must preserve the verifier constraints: do not hand-edit generated `docs/env-vars.md`; put semantics in an authoritative operator source and generate a link, or extend curated generator metadata. Describe arbitration narrowly: baseline suppression for the five mirrored fields, with local-wins behavior for local changes, conflicts, non-arbitrated fields, and missing/incomplete baselines. Describe create-route rollback per consumer because `legacy` does not always mean delete rollback. Also document that explicit `mapping=` and `repo_root=` arguments overwrite corresponding config fields in place. RP20 enters the approved set."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788289802481704001,"uuid":"3aecb542-5838-4882-99ee-4961b6c2966b"}